  "question": {
    "text": "Consider a parallel plate capacitor of area A (of each plate) and separation 'd' between the plates. If $E$ is the electric field and $\\varepsilon_0$ is the permittivity of free space between the plates, then potential energy stored in the capacitor is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "xOh4D",
      "text": "$\\varepsilon_0 \\mathrm{E}^2 \\mathrm{Ad}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "k6VE4",
      "text": "$\\frac{1}{2} \\varepsilon_0 \\mathrm{E}^2 \\mathrm{Ad}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "cw6mZ",
      "text": "$\\frac{1}{4} \\varepsilon_0 \\mathrm{E}^2 \\mathrm{Ad}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "Zu5US",
      "text": "$\\frac{3}{4} \\varepsilon_0 \\mathrm{E}^2 \\mathrm{Ad}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "We know energy density\n$\\rho_{\\mathrm{av}}=\\frac{1}{2} \\varepsilon_0 E^2$\nSo potential energy $=\\rho_{a v} \\times$ Volume\n$\\Rightarrow \\text { P.E. }=\\frac{1}{2} \\varepsilon_0 E^2 A d$",
    "image": null
  },
